PostgreSQL migrations for Tallywise.

Run from backend with the project virtual environment, or specify
-c backend/alembic.ini when running from the repository root.
Connection settings come from config.py, not the placeholder URL in alembic.ini.

5e649e7423b5 is the original baseline and must not be rewritten after use.
b27f4e9a6c10 aligns SERIAL primary keys with GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY.

Use upgrade head for an empty database. For existing tables, inspect the schema
before stamping the matching revision; stamp does not create or validate tables.
Do not stamp head to skip pending changes. See README.md section 25 for details.

The identity migration targets public and locks all four business tables.
Downgrading to the baseline converts identity columns to SERIAL.
Downgrading to base deletes all four business tables and their data.
